*' Which PlantUML draws this file, and in which order the question is asked.
'
' Worth having as a diagram because the order is the decision: an image that
' was asked for beats a local install, everywhere else the machine wins.

@startuml
title Which PlantUML draws it

skinparam shadowing false
' Four branches side by side is a picture as wide as a desk. Vertically, it
' reads as what it is: a list of questions asked in order.
!pragma useVerticalIf on

start

:open a .puml;

if (an image named — .abydos/tools.json,\nor settings — and a runtime to run it?) then (yes)
  :draw in the container;
  note right
    Pinned beats installed, which is
    the point of pinning: the same file
    should look the same on two machines.
  end note
  stop
elseif (plantuml on the PATH?) then (yes)
  :draw with the command;
  note right
    Homebrew's wrapper script, with
    whatever options it sets.
  end note
  stop
elseif (java, and a jar —\nPLANTUML_JAR or where downloads land?) then (yes)
  :java -jar plantuml.jar;
  stop
else (none of them)
  :say in one sentence what to install;
  note right
    An empty pane tells nobody anything.
  end note
endif

stop

@enduml
